precept ProductCatalog

# A stateless data-only precept governing a single product entry in a catalog.
# A product entry holds identity (SKU, name, description), classification
# (category, brand), pricing (list price and optional cost basis), physical
# attributes (weight, length/width/height), and availability flags.
#
# A product is reference data — it does not have a lifecycle of its own.
# Workflow precepts that consume products (orders, shipments, returns)
# reference a product by SKU and assume its data is valid at every read.
# This precept's job is to ensure the data ever stored on a product is valid.
#
# All fields are writable — the host application's catalog management UI is
# responsible for editing them. Identity fields (Sku, Name) are optional in
# storage but the host should refuse to publish a product without them set.

# Identity
field Sku as string optional maxlength 50 writable
field Name as string optional maxlength 200 writable
field Description as string optional writable

# Classification
field Category as choice of string("Electronics","Clothing","HomeGoods","Grocery","HealthBeauty","SportsOutdoors","Toys","Books","Other") default "Other" writable
field Brand as string optional maxlength 100 writable

# Pricing — list price is in the catalog currency.
field CatalogCurrency as currency default 'USD' writable
field ListPrice as money in 'USD' default '0.00 USD' nonnegative writable
field CostBasis as money in 'USD' optional writable

# Physical attributes — weight in kilograms, dimensions in centimetres.
field Weight as quantity in 'kg' default '0 kg' nonnegative writable
field Length as quantity in 'cm' default '0 cm' nonnegative writable
field Width as quantity in 'cm' default '0 cm' nonnegative writable
field Height as quantity in 'cm' default '0 cm' nonnegative writable

# Availability flags
field Active as boolean default true writable
field Discontinued as boolean default false writable
field RequiresShipping as boolean default true writable

rule CostBasis <= ListPrice when CostBasis is set because "Cost basis {CostBasis} cannot exceed the list price {ListPrice} — a product cannot be sold at a structural loss"
rule Active == false or Discontinued == false because "An entry cannot be both Active and Discontinued — these are mutually exclusive lifecycle flags"
